# New in XPPAUT 8.1: periodic orbits and phase reduction
# Morris-Lecar (type II), oscillating for i=150.
#
# ---- 1. Periodic orbit:  Initialconds -> (P)eriodic  (keys I P) --------------
#   i=150 oscillates. First Initialconds -> Go (I G) so the trajectory settles.
#   Then I P: finds the period accurately (T = 63.72 here, printed in the
#   terminal), starts at the maximum of the x-axis variable (V), sets
#   Total = T and transient = 0, and draws exactly one period.
#
# ---- 2. Phase reduction:  nUmerics -> Averaging  (keys U A, then the key) ---
#   After step 1 (Total = one period):
#     N  New adj      adjoint Z (the infinitesimal PRC) AND the isostable
#                     quantities of the cycle; Floquet multiplier etc. printed
#     A  Adjoint      load Z into the data browser (plot V vs t: the PRC)
#     I  Isostable    load the isostable response I (new)
#     F  Floquet rho  load the slowest Floquet eigenfunction rho (new)
#     B  B correction load the correction B to the phase response (new)
#     O  Orbit        load the orbit on the adjoint's grid
#     M  Make H       interaction function H for two coupled cells; give the
#                     coupling per equation using primes for the partner,
#                     e.g. for V:  V'-V   and for W:  0
#     2  H2           second-order interaction function H2 (new; needs N and M)
#     P  Parameters   grid steps for the adjoint
#   (Wilson & Ermentrout, PRL 123, 164101 (2019) for H2.)
#
# ---- 3. AUTO: Hopf type (sub/supercritical) and GH points -------------------
#   Parameters: set i=0. Initialconds -> New: V=-60.899, W=0.014873 (rest).
#   File -> Auto. Run -> Steady state: Hopf points (HB) near i=102 and i=235.
#   Grab (Tab to an HB point, Enter). Set Parameter: Par2 = gca and
#   Axes -> Two par (x: i, y: gca), then Run -> Two param.
#   New: on the two-parameter Hopf curve, supercritical parts keep the usual
#   Hopf colour and SUBCRITICAL parts (first Lyapunov coefficient l1 > 0) are
#   drawn in PURPLE; where l1 changes sign a dot labelled "GH" (generalised
#   Hopf / Bautin point) is drawn.
#
dv/dt=(i+gl*(vl-v)+gk*w*(vk-v)+gca*minf(v)*(vca-v))/c
dw/dt=lamw(v)*(winf(v)-w)
minf(v)=.5*(1+tanh((v-v1)/v2))
winf(v)=.5*(1+tanh((v-v3)/v4))
lamw(v)=phi*cosh((v-v3)/(2*v4))
# i first so AUTO uses it; gca among the first 8 so it can be Par2
param i=150
param gca=4,vk=-84,vl=-60,vca=120,gk=8,gl=2,c=20
param v1=-1.2,v2=18,v3=2,v4=30,phi=.04
v(0)=-60.899
w(0)=0.014873
@ total=1000, dt=0.1, bounds=10000, maxstor=20000
@ xp=v, yp=w, xlo=-80, xhi=60, ylo=-0.05, yhi=0.6
@ autovar=v, autoxmin=0, autoxmax=300, autoymin=-80, autoymax=60
@ parmin=-10, parmax=300, ntst=50, nmax=2000, npr=50
@ ds=0.1, dsmin=0.001, dsmax=5, normmin=0, normmax=1000
done
